  "notes": "Docker Worker Exit Pattern root cause fixed. Problem: Container SIGKILL (exit 137, OOM kill) bypasses all shell traps — the container's EXIT trap never runs, leaving no .result file. Fix: Added host-side fallback in monitorContainer() — when docker wait reports non-zero exit and no .result file exists, the host writes a fallback NO_GO result with exitCode. This ensures result-collector always finds a .result file. Added 4 tests covering SIGKILL, normal exit, SIGTERM, and OOM scenarios. Pre-existing test failures in tests/unit/spawn-backend-docker.test.ts (--time=10 vs --time=15 mismatch from Sprint 139) are not caused by this change. tsc --noEmit PASS.",
